    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** anchors our offensive ceiling with an elite 68.27 projection. Facing a favorable matchup against Corbin (4.62 xERA), he benefits significantly from his leadoff placement and the SP\u2019s poor xERA, making him our primary engine for the stolen base category, which remains the scarcest commodity for the Zebras. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (66.41) and **Yordan Alvarez** (66.32) are must-starts. **Trea Turner** specifically benefits from the slow delivery of Peralta, providing a prime window for stolen base attempts, while **Yordan Alvarez** maintains an elite 0.450 xwOBA despite the platoon disadvantage, proving his ability to transcend matchup quality.\n\nThe benching of **Gary Sanchez** (39.85) was our most difficult decision, as he landed just a fraction of a point below our strict 40-point efficiency floor. While his power upside is theoretically valuable, his poor BvP metrics against Sale and an elite opposing xERA made him too risky for our game cap conservation strategy. **Carson Benge** (38.60) was similarly squeezed out due to a tough draw against S\u00e1nchez and a negative platoon split. Conversely, **Junior Caminero** (60.66) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (60.74) comfortably cleared the threshold, with **Kazuma Okamoto** gaining significant value from his matchup against Rea, who presents a soft landing spot for our middle-order production.\n\nWe are monitoring the situational risks across the board, particularly for **Dillon Dingler** (52.11) and **Casey Schmitt** (44.51). **Dillon Dingler** faces the difficult Newcomb, and his score is heavily buoyed by his #2 spot in the order rather than pure matchup dominance. **Casey Schmitt** remains a marginal play; while he holds a dynamic platoon edge, his low-order placement and the elite hold capabilities of Meyer keep his upside capped. We will continue to prioritize high-speed threats like **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Trea Turner** to maintain our competitive edge in stolen bases, keeping our rostered assets like **Colt Keith** and **Lars Nootbaar** in reserve should injury or late lineup shifts necessitate a pivot.",
